==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Croco]]s spawn after 4 seconds<sup>120f</sup>, delay 3~8 seconds<sup>90f~240f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Croco]]s spawn after 6 seconds<sup>180f</sup>, delay 4~10 seconds<sup>120f~300f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Croco]]s spawn after 8 seconds<sup>240f</sup>, delay 5~12 seconds<sup>150f~360f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Gory Dark]]s spawn after 12 seconds<sup>360f</sup>, delay 40~45 seconds<sup>1,200f~1,350f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 85% HP:
**Infinite [[Gory Dark]]s spawn, delay 40~45 seconds<sup>1,200f~1,350f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 70% HP:
**1 [[Croco]] spawns as the boss.
**Infinite [[Shadow Boxer K]]s spawn, delay 53.33~60 seconds<sup>1,600f~1,800f</sup>.
**Infinite [[Dark Otter]]s spawn, delay 75 seconds<sup>2,250f</sup>.
**1 [[Heavy Assault C.A.T. (Enemy)|Heavy Assault C.A.T.]] spawns.
**1 [[Heavy Assault C.A.T. (Enemy)|Heavy Assault C.A.T.]] spawns.

==Strategy==
To beat this stage, you will need crowd-controllers against the [[:Category:Dark Enemies|Dark Enemies]]. A very strong option here is [[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Pizza Cat]], or a combination of [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Cyborg Cat]] and [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]] if you don't own Pizza Cat, although the Dark enemies will be a bit harder to deal with.

To deal with the two Heavy Assault C.A.T.s, you'll need to use units that outrange it such as [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Crazed Bahamut Cat]] and [[Ururun Wolf (Special Cat)|Ururun Cat]] as well as some meatshields to kill them thanks to their surprisingly high standing range.

